Input: {"question": "When did Louis Alexandre die?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d00", "start": 0, "end": 230, "text": "to his will stating that if all legitimate members of the House of Bourbon, both those descended from Louis and more distant kinsmen, died out, the throne of France could be inherited by the duc du Maine and the comte de Toulouse."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d00", "start": 231, "end": 425, "text": "The decision was reversed after the death of Louis XIV when Louis Alexandre's cousin, Philippe II, Duke of Orléans, as the new regent, had the \"Parlement de Paris\" void that portion of the will."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d00", "start": 426, "end": 502, "text": "The comte de Toulouse died at the Château de Rambouillet on 1 December 1737."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d00", "start": 503, "end": 564, "text": "He was buried in the village 12th century Saint-Lubin church."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 0, "end": 83, "text": ", duc de Chartres , ( later duc d'Orléans ) , the Regent of France under Louis XV ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 84, "end": 95, "text": "Had issue ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 96, "end": 204, "text": "Louis-Alexandre de Bourbon , comte de Toulouse 6 June 1678 1 December 1737 Legitimised on 22 November 1681 ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 205, "end": 333, "text": "Held numerous offices , of which : Admiral of France , Governor of Guyenne , Governor of Brittany , and Grand-Veneur de France ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 334, "end": 394, "text": "Was also duc de Damville , de Rambouillet et de Penthièvre ."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 395, "end": 406, "text": "Had issue ."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 407, "end": 449, "text": "Founder of the House of Bourbon-Toulouse ."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d01", "start": 450, "end": 540, "text": "Paternal legitimate half-siblings - by Marie-Thérèse d'Autriche , Infanta of Spain , Queen"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d02", "start": 0, "end": 615, "text": "in Integrated Authority File retrieved 15 December 2014 date of death 1 December 1737 Gregorian 7 references stated in Integrated Authority File retrieved 28 April 2014 stated in BnF authorities Bibliothèque nationale de France ID 12570085z retrieved 10 October 2015 stated in SNAC SNAC ARK ID w6h13z0j subject named as Louis Alexandre , Count of Toulouse retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in Find a Grave Find a Grave memorial ID 84676726 subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in The Peerage The Peerage person ID p10526.htm # i105257 subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03", "start": 0, "end": 164, "text": "Extinction date 15 June 1745 The count of Toulouse (Occitan: comte de Tolosa, French: comte de Toulouse) was the ruler of Toulouse during the 8th to 13th centuries."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03", "start": 165, "end": 328, "text": "Originating as vassals of the Frankish kings, [1] the hereditary counts ruled the city of Toulouse and its surrounding county from the late 9th century until 1270."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03", "start": 329, "end": 521, "text": "The counts and other family members were also at various times counts of Quercy, Rouergue, Albi, and Nîmes, and sometimes margraves (military defenders of the Holy Roman Empire) of the region."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03", "start": 522, "end": 614, "text": "The last known count, Louis Alexandre, died on 15 June 1745, marking the end of the lineage."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d04", "start": 0, "end": 604, "text": "of birth Versailles, Yvelines, Île-de-France, France Death 1 January 1738 People who died on this day Place of death Rambouillet, canton of Rambouillet, arrondissement of Rambouillet, Yvelines Age 59 years Family Mother : Françoise-Athénaïs, marquise de Montespan Father : Louis XIV of France Siblings : Philippe Charles Duke of Anjou Louis Count of Vermandois Louis Auguste Duke of Maine Louis César Count of Vexin Louis François Duke of Anjou Louis Grand Dauphin Louis Antoine de Pardaillan de Gondrin Princess Anne Élisabeth of France Marie Thérèse Madame Royale Louise Marie Anne de Bourbon Françoise"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d05", "start": 0, "end": 159, "text": ", in 1783 , his remains , as well as the remains of other family members , were transferred by his son to the chapel of the Collégiale Saint-Étienne de Dreux ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d05", "start": 160, "end": 307, "text": "This was desecrated in 1793 and the bodies of ten family members thrown in a mass grave at the Chanoines cemetery of the Collégiale Saint-Étienne ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d05", "start": 308, "end": 446, "text": "In 1816 , his granddaughter Louise Marie Adélaïde de Bourbon , Duchess of Orléans , had a new chapel built at the site of the mass grave ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d05", "start": 447, "end": 509, "text": "In 1830 , her son Louis-Philippe I , King of the French , made"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d06", "start": 0, "end": 679, "text": ", Comte de Toulouse retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in Brockhaus Enzyklopädie Brockhaus Enzyklopädie online ID bourbon-louis-alexandre-de subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in Genealogics genealogics.org person ID I00004405 subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon de Toulouse de Penthièvre place of death Rambouillet 1 reference stated in Integrated Authority File retrieved 31 December 2014 place of burial Dreux Royal Chapel 0 references father Louis XIV of France 0 references mother Madame de Montespan 0 references sibling Princess Anne Élisabeth of France 0 references Marie Thérèse , Madame Royale 0 references Louis Antoine de"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d02:c0", "entity": "Louis Alexandre", "scope": "Date of death", "claim": "Louis Alexandre died on 1 December 1737.", "answer": "1 December 1737", "quote": "in Integrated Authority File retrieved 15 December 2014 date of death 1 December 1737 Gregorian 7 references stated in Integrated Authority File retrieved 28 April 2014 stated in BnF authorities Bibliothèque nationale de France ID 12570085z retrieved 10 October 2015 stated in SNAC SNAC ARK ID w6h13z0j subject named as Louis Alexandre , Count of Toulouse retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in Find a Grave Find a Grave memorial ID 84676726 subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon retrieved 9 October 2017 stated in The Peerage The Peerage person ID p10526.htm # i105257 subject named as Louis Alexandre de Bourbon", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d03:c0", "entity": "Louis Alexandre", "scope": "Death date", "claim": "The last known count, Louis Alexandre, died on 15 June 1745.", "answer": "15 June 1745", "quote": "The last known count, Louis Alexandre, died on 15 June 1745, marking the end of the lineage.", "original_document_number": 4}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0021-ea1c12a29ed3:d04:c0", "entity": "Louis Alexandre", "scope": "Death date", "claim": "Louis Alexandre died on 1 January 1738.", "answer": "1 January 1738", "quote": "of birth Versailles, Yvelines, Île-de-France, France Death 1 January 1738 People who died on this day Place of death Rambouillet, canton of Rambouillet, arrondissement of Rambouillet, Yvelines Age 59 years Family Mother : Françoise-Athénaïs, marquise de Montespan Father : Louis XIV of France Siblings : Philippe Charles Duke of Anjou Louis Count of Vermandois Louis Auguste Duke of Maine Louis César Count of Vexin Louis François Duke of Anjou Louis Grand Dauphin Louis Antoine de Pardaillan de Gondrin Princess Anne Élisabeth of France Marie Thérèse Madame Royale Louise Marie Anne de Bourbon Françoise", "original_document_number": 5}], "current_answers": ["1 December 1737", "15 June 1745", "1 January 1738"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "1 December 1737", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "15 June 1745", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "1 January 1738", "origin": "initial"}]}

